  The draft says the fraud was against 'Ambattur' and that Satya is a jewellery shop owner's counterpart; the article says Satya is from Mannadi, Puthu Street, but the draft's reel_script and slides say 'Satya (51 years old)' is 'Mannadi, Puthu Street' — this is consistent, however the caption says Satya was 'ஏமாற்றப்பட்டார்' and the 'நகைகளை மீட்டுத் தருவதாக' wording misrepresents the article, which says Anand received Rs 50 lakh to be given to Thendral Anand and Gokul, not that he promised to recover jewellery
  The draft states the fraud accomplice Palani was arrested and released on bail; the article says the police arrested Palani and released him on bail, which matches, but the reel_script omits that Thendral Anand and Gokul (who took the jewellery and pledged it) were not mentioned as the ones who gave only Rs 11 lakh in the slides, and the reel_script fails to name them as the parties who received the money — an important fact missing from the reel_script
  The caption and reel_script say 'உடந்தையான பழனி (53 வயது)' while the article calls Palani an accomplice (உடந்தையான) only in the arrest sentence; the draft's 'Ambattur jewellery shop owner arrested' English line and the caption's ' Rs 39 lakh fraud' are consistent, but the caption describes 'நவம்பர் 25ஆம் தேதி ஆனந்த் கைது' while the article says the arrest was made today (நவ.,25), which is fine
  The reel_script states Anand was arrested on 'நவம்பர் 25ஆம் தேதி' with no year, while the caption adds '2026' as the posting date, which is an invented year in the article-derived date line
  The slides_spec 'அம்பத்தூர் குற்றப்பிரிவு போலீசார் விசாரணை' and 'ஆனந்த் சிறையில் அடைக்கப்பட்டார்' are supported, but the cause line 'அடகு நகைகளை மீட்க ரூ.50 லட்சம் பணம் கொடுக்கப்பட்டது' misstates the purpose: the article says Satya gave Rs 50 lakh to jeweller Anand, not for recovering pledged jewellery by the Rs 50 lakh payer
